entries.detail:
Ran swiftlint's opening_brace/closure_parameter_position rules across all 59 .swift files in the eight target directories (0 violations reported, since that lint only checks brace spacing/positioning, not statement count after the brace), then manually grepped for `{ ... ; ... }` patterns (multiple statements crammed onto the opening-brace line, separated by semicolons) across the same scope. Found several genuine offenses where more than one statement follows the opening brace on the same line, which is not covered by the One-Statement-Per-Line exception (that exception only permits a single statement to stay on the brace's line) and is not a closure-with-`in` or an empty `{}`. Clearest example: akin-server-side/Sources/App/Matching/EntitlementResolver.swift:51 - `public init(tier: Tier, expiresAt: Date?) { self.tier = tier; self.expiresAt = expiresAt }` -> break after the opening brace: `public init(tier: Tier, expiresAt: Date?) {
    self.tier = tier
    self.expiresAt = expiresAt
}`. Additional instances of the same offense in scope: akin-server-side/Sources/App/Subscriptions/NotificationFanOut.swift:155 (`catch { failures.append((recipient, error)); continue }`), akin-server-side/Sources/App/Matching/AlgorithmSelector.swift:35, akin-server-side/Sources/App/Matching/AdFeedBuilder.swift:25 (`if case .ad = self { return true }; return false`), akin-server-side/Sources/App/Matching/EntitlementResolver+DB.swift:15 (three case statements after the switch's `{`), :168, and :299, akin-server-side/Sources/App/Matching/MatchingAlgorithm.swift:21, and akin-server-side/Sources/App/Matching/VenueNegotiation.swift:20.
